      {
        "id": 147227,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-09T05:10:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>dpt wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>I can knit horizontal cables.(Most knitted cables you've seen are what I'd call \"vertical\", where the direction of the braiding runs perpendicular to the rows of knitting. I worked out how to braid the knitted rows.)\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nOoh, can you teach me how to do that?&nbsp; \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It requires some planning. You start knitting a stockinette background (pure knit stiches). Then you knit a few rows of purl stitch and one row of knit. You then unravel the purl stitches in section, leaving some loose yarn, and pick up the loops at the top of the stockinette section. You then do a few more rows of pure purl stitches, partially on top of the previous purl section and partly on the original stockinette section. Then you re-purl with the loose yarn that resulted from the unravelling.</p>\n<p>Hmm, that comes across really poorly textually.</p>",
