        "created_at": "2015-09-09T15:40:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>. Stomatopods (also called Mantis Shrimp) are generally ridiculous.  The larger ones can strike with the force of a small caliber bullet (and have broken aquariums made of double layered saftey glass!).  Their strikes are so fast that they create cavitation bubbles, which collapse in bright flashes of heat and light that then send shockwaves that can stun fish.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That is the best episode of True Facts!</p>\n<p>Speaking of tin, in vacuum solder will form “tin whiskers” that grow out as thin metal filaments. This was discovered when early spacecraft kept short-circuiting after launch.</p>",
